(label "SDA" (at 109.22 54.61 90) (fields_autoplaced yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c63a7ff5-8201-4f41-b45a-711043482ddd"))
(label "SCL" (at 104.14 62.23 90) (fields_autoplaced yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "dde1d5ce-a984-456b-908d-7088c01bdd04"))
(text "Notes\n1. Power: Nano ESP32 only from USB-C (INIU SnapGo P81 power bank). The Nano 3V3 pin feeds every module. VIN and VUSB unused.\n2. One I2C bus, 400 kHz: LSM6DSOX 0x6A, LIS3MDL 0x1C (unused), MAX30102 0x57, SSD1306 0x3C. Scanned together 2026-11-03; all four ran in firmware/app 2026-11-06.\n3. Pull-ups: 4517 has 10k to 3.3 V; GY-MAX30102 has 4.7k to its own 1.8 V rail. Measure SDA/SCL high level; below 2.5 V remove the MAX30102 pull-ups.\n4. SW1: one kit pushbutton to GND, INPUT_PULLUP on D2. Short press start/pause/resume, hold 1.5 s end (firmware/app). Tested 2026-11-06.\n5. LED1 on D7 through 220 ohm; use a red or yellow LED at 3.3 V. BZ1 is optional: firmware/app compiles with USE_BUZZER 0, D5 held LOW.\n6. 4517 pins follow the 4209 STEMMA QT cable colours. MAX30102 INT and 4517 INT not wired (polling). D8/D9 reserved for them.\nSource: hardware/wiring/README.md, firmware/app/app.ino. Redrawn in KiCad from Julia's EasyEDA V2.0 (2026-11-08); regenerate with gen_kicad_sch.py." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 30.48 163.83 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9224f28b-4649-4499-886c-68b6b14600bd"))
